# Ruling 10: module 1's migrations run exactly once and in order; a migration edited after it was applied is REFUSED. The fault disables the checksum comparison in the runner (the file is
# edited, the database is not): the runner accepts the changed file and the test must say so. Real Postgres, the real runner code.
GATE=m1-tracker-checksum
TARGET=module:coldmail-verify
SETUP=
STEP=go test TestMigrate_ChangedFileIsRefused (a changed migration is refused, the database unchanged)
CMD=cd control-plane && TM_TEST_DATABASE_URL="$FAULT_ADMIN_DSN" go test -count=1 -v -run '^TestMigrate_ChangedFileIsRefused$' ./internal/migrate/
MESSAGE=--- FAIL: TestMigrate_ChangedFileIsRefused
MESSAGE=a changed migration was accepted
